      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the total number of green tiles and blue tiles in the original figure and then the total number of green tiles and blue tiles in the new figure after adding a border of green tiles. Finally, we will find the difference between the total number of green tiles and blue tiles in the new figure.\n\nFirst, let's analyze the original figure:\n\n1. There are 13 blue tiles.\n2. There are 6 green tiles.\n\nThe figure is composed of:\n- 4 equilateral triangles at the corners,\n- 8 equilateral triangles sharing sides with the equilateral triangles at the corners.\n\nLet's visualize the structure:\n- A central equilateral triangle with side length equal to two green tiles.\n- Surrounding the central triangle, there are four equilateral triangles each with side length equal to the side length of the central triangle.\n\nEach green tile is surrounded by blue tiles. The central square is entirely made of green tiles. The square contains the 4 central equilateral triangles (corners) and 4 more triangular forms inside each corner (other than the base).\n\nThe resulting arrangement of green tiles in the central larger square is 3 green tiles (each triangle is separated by spaces, forming a larger overall shape). Each of these triangles contributes 2 green tiles regularly, totaling 3+3+3 = 9 green tiles.\n\nNext, consider constructing a border layer of green tiles around the figure. This can be expanded 2 squares per side (subtract 2 due to separate boundary), effectively increasing green tiles by an amount of 2×4 (sides) = 8 times sides.\n\nThus, the result of the expansion gives us:\n\\[\n8 \\times 4 = 32\n\\]\n\nAdding them all, we find the total number of green tiles made up of 32.\n\\[\n\\boxed{32}\n\\]\n\nNext calculate the total number of blue tiles by subtracting green tiles from both the original and our expanded structures:\n\\[\n\\text{Blue tiles} = 13\n\\]\nAs separate entities, originally, we have 13 blue tiles.\n\nConsequently, our expanded observation leads to additional structures (total 32):\n\n\\[\n13 + 32 = 45\n\\]\n\nHence, the difference between total number of green and blue tiles:\n\\[\n45 - 36 = \\boxed{9}\n\\]",
