dary. We already have 24 - 9 = 15 tiles (which includes 15 - 3 = 12 more tiles from the additional green parts, adding to 24. With 15 tiles, we have 15*2 - 3 (the 12 tiles already counting the 3 idetcial tiles) = 27, we have which adds to the original 34 vertices.\n\nThus, after adding the border of green tiles, the figure now equals 9 + 24. Finally, there are 27 green tiles.\n\nSince there are 9 blue tiles, the difference in the green and blue tiles is 9 - 24/2 = 7.  \n\nSo, the difference between the total number of green tiles and the total number of blue tiles in the new figure is \\boxed{7}.",
